<!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","align":"full","style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|80","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|80"}}},"layout":{"type":"constrained","contentSize":"820px"}} -->
<section class="wp-block-group alignfull" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80)"><!-- wp:heading {"textAlign":"center","fontSize":"x-large","style":{"spacing":{"margin":{"bottom":"var:preset|spacing|50"}}}} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-x-large-font-size" style="margin-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)">Practical Questions</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:group {"style":{"spacing":{"blockGap":"var:preset|spacing|20"}},"layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group"><!-- wp:details {"showContent":true,"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" open style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>What If I Don't Want to Work With Plant Medicine?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">That is completely okay. At Lumina, participation in plant medicine ceremonies is encouraged, but never required if a guest is feeling apprehensive.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Guests who choose the non-medicine path remain fully included in the retreat experience — the opening and closing circles, daily Qi Gong, teachings, meditation, group integration, community activities, and the complete 4-E Elemental Wisdom Process. You are held within the same supportive container and receive the same personal guidance.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Healing does not belong to any one modality. While plant medicine can be a powerful catalyst, lasting transformation ultimately comes from your willingness to look honestly at yourself and engage fully with the process. At Lumina, there is no "lesser" path. There is only your path.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>Where will we stay?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">On-site, together, in a private retreat center, in either a private or shared room. The retreat center is located in the Verde Valley, on the river, about 30 minutes from Sedona.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>How do I get there?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Most guests fly into Phoenix Sky Harbor, which has the widest selection of flights — about an hour-and-a-half drive to Sedona. Flagstaff is closer, with a beautiful hour's drive down the canyon, but offers fewer flights. Travel isn't included, but we'll point you to shuttle options and directions.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>How many guests attend each retreat?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Lumina intentionally keeps retreat groups small (12 maximum) to ensure a more personal, supportive, and individualized experience. This allows for meaningful connections, deeper group cohesion, and greater access to guidance and support throughout the retreat.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>What's the deposit and cancellation policy?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">A $500 non-refundable deposit secures your place, with the balance due one week before the retreat. If you've paid in full and need to cancel, we refund your payment minus the $500 deposit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>Is Ayahuasca safe?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Safety is one of our highest priorities. All guests complete a detailed health screening and intake process before acceptance. Certain medications, medical conditions, and psychological conditions may require additional review or may not be compatible with participation. Our full approach to safety and care is laid out on our Care Protocol page — the application is the first step in that conversation.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>What makes Lumina different from other retreats?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Many retreats focus primarily on the ceremony experience. At Lumina, we believe the ceremony is only part of the journey. Our unique 4-E Elemental Wisdom Process helps guests understand, integrate, and embody what emerges during retreat so the insights become lasting change rather than temporary experiences.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>What if I've never done Ayahuasca before?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Many of our guests are first-time participants. You do not need any previous experience. Prior to retreat, you will receive preparation materials and guidance to help you understand the process and prepare both mentally and physically. Our team is available to answer questions before arrival and support you throughout.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>What if I'm nervous?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Almost everyone feels some level of nervousness before attending. Stepping into the unknown can feel vulnerable, especially when entering a process of deep self-exploration. Nervousness is often a sign that something meaningful matters to you. Our role is not to push you beyond your readiness, but to provide a safe, supportive, and compassionate environment where you can move at a pace that feels appropriate for you.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>What happens during the ceremonies?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Each ceremony is conducted within a carefully held and intentional setting. While every person's experience is unique, ceremonies may involve deep emotional insight, personal reflection, healing experiences, spiritual exploration, or a greater understanding of recurring patterns in life. Guests are encouraged to approach the experience with openness rather than expectation.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>What is the 4-E Elemental Wisdom Process?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">The 4-E Process is Lumina's unique framework for transformation and integration. It helps guests identify the underlying structures beneath recurring emotional patterns, limiting beliefs, and life challenges. Through guided inquiry and experiential practices, participants learn to work with these patterns consciously rather than remaining unconsciously driven by them. It is introduced during retreat and becomes a lifelong tool.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>What is included in the four-week integration program?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Every guest receives private sessions across four weeks of post-retreat integration support. This period helps participants apply what they have learned to everyday life, deepen their understanding of the retreat experience, and continue working with the 4-E Process. Integration is often where the most lasting transformation occurs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>What should I bring?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Prior to retreat, you will receive a detailed preparation handbook and packing list. In general, guests should bring comfortable clothing, layers for changing temperatures, walking shoes, a flashlight, personal toiletries, a water bottle, and an open mind.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"width":"1px","radius":"10px"},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|30","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|30","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"borderColor":"border"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-border-color has-border-border-color" style="border-width:1px;border-radius:10px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><summary>What if difficult emotions arise?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"muted"} -->
<p class="has-muted-color has-text-color">Difficult emotions are a natural part of healing and transformation. Rather than viewing these experiences as problems, we see them as opportunities for greater understanding, compassion, and freedom. Guests are supported throughout the retreat with guidance, community, and integration practices designed to help them navigate whatever emerges. You do not have to do it alone.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></section>
<!-- /wp:group -->
